  "screenwriter_raw": "{\n  \"pseudos\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"p1\",\n      \"text\": \"In the grand carnival of corporate reinvention, the tax-software company delivered a punchline to its workforce. The chief executive announced a painful but necessary reinvention, a spectacle where roughly 17% of the workforce becomes the collateral of a 'strategic' AI circus. The show must go on, but the tents are folding in Reno and Woodland Hills.\",\n      \"fit\": 0.88,\n      \"center\": \"why-1\",\n      \"channel\": \"toned\",\n      \"source\": {\n        \"fragments\": [\"why-1\", \"how-0\", \"result-0\", \"how-2\"]\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"p2\",\n      \"text\": \"The solemn messenger of 'necessary' corporate theater, the CEO, delivered the viral moment of mass job cuts. To co-locate teams and accelerate AI-driven product work, about 3,000 full-time roles were staged for elimination. The 3,000 caught in the corporate farce were offered a severance package as a parting joke.\",\n      \"fit\": 0.85,\n      \"center\": \"how-0\",\n      \"channel\": \"toned\",\n      \"source\": {\n        \"fragments\": [\"how-0\", \"why-0\", \"result-1\", \"how-1\"]\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"p3\",\n      \"text\": \"The chief executive announced the grand vanishing act of 3,000 jobs, a decision communicated to staff as a business strategy. The workers affected were offered a compensation offer, a financial package of 16 weeks' base pay, while the company's offices in Nevada and California wound down operations.\",\n      \"fit\": 0.72,\n      \"center\": \"who-1\",\n      \"channel\": \"toned\",\n      \"source\": {\n        \"fragments\": [\"how-0\", \"why-0\", \"result-3\", \"how-2\"]\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}",
